  "prompt": "[system]\nYou generate compact online DVRP dispatch policies that minimize TTT (last-truck return time).\n\n[user]\nImplement exactly this interface:\n\ndef choose_next_customer(\n    current_position: np.ndarray,        # (2,) the deciding truck's position\n    depot_position: np.ndarray,          # (2,)\n    truck_positions: np.ndarray,         # (n_trucks, 2) all trucks\n    available_customers: np.ndarray,     # (n_available, 2) revealed unserved customers\n) -> int | None:\n\nRules:\n- DVRP is an online dispatch problem; the objective is to minimize TTT, defined here as the last-truck return time.\n- Decide which customer the active truck (at current_position) should head to next.\n- Return an index into available_customers, or None to wait at the current position.\n- If available_customers is empty, return None.\n- The function is stateless across calls; treat each call as a one-shot decision with the snapshot given.\n- Do not assume coordinates beyond what is passed; do not hard-code instance sizes, truck counts, or dataset details.\n- Do not read/write files, use network, spawn subprocesses, or call external solvers.\n- No module-level mutable globals; the function may be called many times across instances.\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT MODE: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000010 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Candidate's simplified heuristic worsened gap to 42.83 (parent 36.16), indicating that ignoring truck competition harms last-return time.\n- Aim: Reintroduce truck-competition awareness via a distance-to-nearest-other-truck term, balancing depot distance and isolation to reduce long detours.\n\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000010: FarFirstDispatch\nStatus: valid; Gap: 42.8251%\nThought: Dispatch to customer maximizing dist_to_depot minus dist_to_truck, favoring far-from-depot customers that are close to the truck. Wait if no customers.\nMean gap: 42.825122380828525\nMean TTT: 4.195611391037662\nGap by instance size: {'50': 42.825122380828525}\nTTT by instance size: {'50': 4.195611391037662}\nCode:\n```python\ndef choose_next_customer(current_position, depot_position, truck_positions, available_customers):\n    if len(available_customers) == 0:\n        return None\n    best_idx = None\n    best_cost = -float('inf')\n    for i, cust in enumerate(available_customers):\n        dist_to_truck = np.linalg.norm(current_position - cust)\n        dist_to_depot = np.linalg.norm(depot_position - cust)\n        cost = dist_to_depot - dist_to_truck\n        if cost > best_cost:\n            best_cost = cost\n            best_idx = i\n    return best_idx\n```\n\nMinimize TTT: the time until the last truck returns to the depot. This is the only optimization goal.\n\nInternal check before final JSON: correct choose_next_customer signature, returns None or a valid\navailable_customers index, handles empty available_customers no I/O/network/subprocesses.\n\nReturn one JSON object and nothing else:\n{\n  \"name\": \"snake_case_or_title\",\n  \"thought\": \"brief public summary of the dispatch rule, tie-break, and wait condition\",\n  \"code\": \"complete Python code as a JSON string\"\n}",
